I've written the session plan: two task files and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. The commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is listed in .gitignore. The instructions allow for that with || true, so the files are on disk and nothing is committed.

Both tasks fix #1211, the data-loss bug the assessment reproduced on the built binary: /save a.md replaced the user's a.md with [] and gave no warning. This also counts as the backlog drain, since there are 15 open agent-self issues, more than the 12 limit.

• Task 1 (Part of #1211): `/save`.
  • Rule: /save refuses to replace an existing file unless --force is given, with one exception. It can silently replace the file this same yoyo process last saved with /save or read with /load.
  • Why the exception: without it, saving your own session a second time would need --force every time. Another session's save file or README.md is still protected.
  • Implementation: it copies how /export does it (create_new, the existing check function, tests in a separate file so commands_session.rs stays under its 2,000-line limit).
  • Checks: it tests that the command printed in the refusal parses back to the same path with --force, runs a break-it-then-restore check on the refusal, and updates the help text and docs.
• Task 2 (Fixes #1211): `/spawn -o`.
  • Behaviour: it refuses an existing output file before the sub-agent starts, so a refused run costs no tokens. It also uses create_new when writing, so a file created while the sub-agent was running isn't replaced.
  • Search for other cases: before the Fixes push, it lists every file write in src/ and reports how many of them write to a path the user typed.
  • Fallback: if task 1 didn't land, this task's title switches to "Part of".
  • File-size limit: commands_spawn.rs is 4,566 lines against its recorded 4,570 (the test fails beyond 100 lines over that). New tests go in a separate file, and the recorded number gets updated if needed.

Other issues:
• #1186 (Fable 5.2 pricing): still waiting on the yoagent fix. I checked, and yoagent 0.27.9 still has no claude-fable-5-2 row.
• #1202 (bash safety): on hold. The open question there is whether a command yoyo can't parse should still run automatically under --yes, -p or with no terminal, and @yuanhao hasn't answered it.
• #1210, #1184, #1208: deferred to later sessions.

